#### [MODIFY] [customer.controller.ts](file:///f:/Project/DilMart-main/backend/src/modules/customer/customer.controller.ts)

Add `GET /customer/home` endpoint:

```typescript
@Get('home')
async getHome(
  @Query('city') city?: string,
  @Query('business_type') businessType?: string,
  @Query('latitude') latitude?: string,
  @Query('longitude') longitude?: string,
) { ... }
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This endpoint does NOT require authentication (`@Roles(CUSTOMER)` on controller). The `/barbershops` endpoint is also public. Should `/customer/home` remain under the `@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard, RolesGuard)` + `@Roles(CUSTOMER)` that the whole controller has? Or should we create a separate public controller?
> 
> **Recommendation**: Keep it under `CustomerController` with auth guard — same as current behavior where `useHomeRecommendations` calls the authenticated `api.barbershops.list()`.

